meta {
  name: Suggest what to link to an external service
  type: http
  seq: 28
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/monitoring-checks/:monitoringCheck_id/link-suggestions
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  monitoringCheck_id: 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  For a monitor that watches a third-party status page: your DNS zones, domains, servers and monitors that your own records tie to that service and that are not linked to it yet, each with the `reason` it was found by. A status page component is suggested only when the monitor that feeds it is already linked to the service or suggested here, never because of its name; its `reason` has `signal` `component`, the component as `subject` and that monitor as `detail`. Link one with the link endpoint above. Empty for a service InfraNest does not recognise and nothing of yours is linked to.

  Scope: `monitoring.read`
}
